From: Armada Linux H.265 publisher
Subject: [PATCH] Advertise the primary codec for single-layer tracks

LiveKit's TrackPublishedResponse does not contain the top-level MIME type yet.
The Go SDK consequently learns a publication's MIME type from SimulcastCodecs,
but PublishTrack only fills that field when a backup codec is present. A normal
single-layer H.265 track is therefore treated as an unknown primary codec when
the server sends a subscribed-quality update.

Populate the same primary codec descriptor for an ordinary video track. This
does not add simulcast or a backup encoder; it preserves the codec metadata the
SDK itself needs to classify the already-published track.

--- a/vendor/github.com/livekit/server-sdk-go/v2/localparticipant.go
+++ b/vendor/github.com/livekit/server-sdk-go/v2/localparticipant.go
@@ -145,4 +145,13 @@ func (p *LocalParticipant) prepareTrackPublication(track webrtc.TrackLocal, opt
                 Height:  uint32(opts.VideoHeight),
             },
         }
+		if primaryCodec.MimeType != "" {
+			// TrackPublishedResponse does not carry TrackInfo.MimeType yet.
+			// Supplying the primary descriptor here makes the server echo it in
+			// TrackInfo.Codecs, which is how LocalTrackPublication.MimeType
+			// classifies subscribed-quality updates.
+			req.SimulcastCodecs = []*livekit.SimulcastCodec{
+				{Codec: primaryCodec.MimeType, Cid: track.ID()},
+			}
+		}
     }
